From 0f11b97be6db17ef5ab96a4d79b6222a568a3bd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arena-agent <arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 14:08:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MaskConj select vectorization, GEP rematerialization for
 remainder bases, FMA SIB scratch-collision fix
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

vectorize.rs: MaskConj{is_and,l,r} folds nested shared-arm selects over compare
masks into one packed And/Or + a single blend (case-fold family: 3.5-4x vs main
at -O3 v3, eqor now beats gcc). MAP_MAX_NODES 12->16. GetElementPtr joins the
clonable pure-chain nodes in plan_invariant_chain (with set_cloned_dest and a
hand-rewrite of the cloned GEP base, which for_each_operand_mut never visits):
their dominance gate had declined every matmul FMA transform (bench matmul
3.13x slower than main); with the arm, 4x vfmadd231pd returns at parity.

x86 intrinsics: FmaF64x4HoistedSIB resolved operand homes via operand_reg but
reloaded home-less operands into fixed rax/rdx/rsi scratches — a home in a later
scratch register got clobbered, emitting vmovupd (%rsi,%rsi) (address 2*j) and
miscompiling remainder-shaped FMA loops (segfault at 2*j; latent on main under
register pressure). Reloads now pick a pool register that is no operand home
and no already-chosen destination.

Tests: vectorize_mask_conj (positive/anti shapes, n=0..33 sweeps) and
vectorize_fma_remainder_257 (odd-N remainder differential, single instance).
